      "message": "A slightly more efficient version using non-public APIs relies on `SkImage_Base::getROPixels()` to avoid allocating a new SkImage:\n\n```\n    SkBitmap bm;\n    if (!as_IB(img)-\u003egetROPixels(ctx, \u0026bm)) {\n        return nullptr;\n    }\n    return Encode(bm.pixmap(), options);\n```\n\nThis is the pattern used in pretty much all other encoders, e.g. https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/encode/SkWebpEncoderImpl.cpp;drc\u003d746b6b8836d1f832ade517ba09d5149cbb58ec3f;l\u003d263",
